link { url = "/docs/gpu", "Run a numerical function on the GPU" }

h2 { "What runs where" }

CPU programs run on the supported macOS, Linux and Windows targets. Apple Metal is the current GPU backend on macOS 26 or newer with Apple silicon. GPU execution supports numerical scalars and dense tensors; a CPU feature is not automatically a GPU feature.

callout { type = info, "This documentation describes the native development preview. CUDA, distributed execution, model loading and a full LLM inference runtime are separate work. See the GPU guide for the implemented numerical scope." }

